    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n43920" root="&#xA;                        نزك&#xA;                    " body-key="n1">
                        
                            <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">نِزْكٌ</span></b> 
                         The <i>penis</i> (<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ذَكَر</span>, S, K, i. e. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">قَضِيب</span>, TA)
of the <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ضَبّ</span> (S, K) and of the <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">وَرَل</span>: (K: [in the
CK, <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">والوَركُ</span> is erroneously put for <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">والوَرَلِ</span>:)
accord. to the assertion of the Arabs, (S,) it
(S, K,) the former, (S,) as also the <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حِرْذَوْن</span>,
(Msb voce <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حرذون</span>,) has two penes (<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">نِزْكَانِ</span>);
(S, K, TA;) and the female has <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">قُرْنَتَانِ</span>, i. e.
[two wombs] <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رَحِمَانِ</span>. (TA.)

